:name: STM32F4 Discovery UART2 Test
:description: Runs an ELF on STM32F4 Discovery and shows UART2 output

# 1. Define the variable for your ELF file
# REPLACE 'testEMU.elf' with the actual path to your file
$bin?=@micdebug.elf

# 2. Create the machine
mach create "stm32f4_disco"

# 3. Load the standard STM32F4 Discovery platform
# Renode includes this platform definition by default
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery.repl

# 4. Open the UART2 Analyzer window
# On the STM32F4 Discovery, UART2 is usually the main output
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2



# 5. Load your binary
sysbus LoadELF $bin
# Enable ITM on the CPU
machine EnableProfiler @itm_output.log


sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.usart2
# 6. Start the simulation
start